# Chronicleaf Community operator values. Names only: no working secret belongs in
# this file, in version control, or in any image. Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# CHRONICLEAF_APP_PORT        Host port for the loopback application binding.
#                              Defaults to 5080 when unset; set it only to avoid a
#                              collision (parallel verification runs do this).
# CHRONICLEAF_DB_PASSWORD      PostgreSQL password for the `chronicleaf` role. Any length the
#                              operator chooses; used by both services from this one value.
# CHRONICLEAF_ACCESS_TOKEN_HASH  SHA-256 hex (64 lower-case hex characters) of the operator's
#                              random setup token of at least 32 random bytes. The plaintext
#                              token is never configured, stored or logged; it is exchanged
#                              once for a session cookie. Generate with:
#                                openssl rand -hex 32 | xxd -r -p | sha256sum
#                              Changing this value revokes every existing session on next start.
# CHRONICLEAF_PUBLIC_ORIGIN    The exact origin the browser uses, e.g.
#                              http://127.0.0.1:5080 for a loopback install or
#                              https://chronicleaf.example behind a reverse proxy.
#                              A mutation from any other origin is refused with 403.
# CHRONICLEAF_ENCRYPTION_KEY_FILE  Host path to the 32-byte AES-256 operator key file,
#                              mounted read-only into the application container. Generate
#                              outside the repository with `umask 177`:
#                                umask 177 && openssl rand -out /run/chronicleaf-encryption.key 32
#                              Until it names a readable 32-byte file, every credential
#                              route refuses with credential_vault_unavailable and nothing
#                              is stored in the clear.
CHRONICLEAF_APP_PORT=
CHRONICLEAF_DB_PASSWORD=
CHRONICLEAF_ACCESS_TOKEN_HASH=
CHRONICLEAF_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=
CHRONICLEAF_ENCRYPTION_KEY_FILE=
